Cell["SpectralElement`", "ContextNameCell"],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["SpectralDomain", "ObjectName"]}}]], "ObjectNameGrid",
  CellID->200000023],
Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{"", Cell[TextData[{
  Cell[BoxData["SpectralDomain[patches, n, opts]"], "InlineFormula"],
  " \[LineSeparator]",
  "SpectralDomain[patches, n, opts] builds a SpectralDiscretization object from a list of CoonsPatch patches, all discretized at the same degree n.  Shared geometric edges are detected by sampling (endpoints plus interior Chebyshev nodes, compared within tolerance), their unknowns are shared (continuous in value), and normal-flux continuity rows are added, so the patches are coupled exactly as in a conforming continuous-Galerkin assembly.  SpectralDomain[region, n] accepts the region shorthands Rectangle[{x1, y1}, {x2, y2}] and Annulus[{r1, r2}, {θ1, θ2}] with r1 > 0, and builds the CoonsPatches automatically; Disk is not supported (the polar map is singular at r = 0, giving a zero Jacobian) and gives SpectralDomain::nreg.  Options include \"InterfaceTolerance\" -> tol and \"BoundaryPredicate\" -> fun."
}]]}}]], "Usage", CellID->982511436]
}, Open]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["Details and Options"], "NotesSection",
  WholeCellGroupOpener->True, CellGroupingRules->{"SectionGrouping", 50},
  CellID->200000024],
Cell[BoxData["SpectralDomain accepts two forms. In the patch-list form the first
          argument is a non-empty list of CoonsPatch objects, all of them at the
          same degree n; version 1 has one n for the whole domain and no per-patch
          grading. In the region-shorthand form the first argument is a region and
          the patches are built for you."], "Notes", CellID->200000025],
Cell[BoxData["Every patch is discretized on the degree-n Chebyshev-Gauss-Lobatto grid in
          each direction, n+1 nodes per direction. ξ is the fast index, and the
          ξ-operator is the second Kronecker argument."], "Notes", CellID->200000026],
Cell[BoxData["Shared edges are detected by sampling, not by bookkeeping. For each
          candidate pair of edges from different patches the endpoints and the
          interior Chebyshev nodes of the two traces are compared, and they match
          when every comparison is within \"InterfaceTolerance\". A matched pair then
          shares one unknown per physical node, so the solution is continuous
          pointwise with no cross-grid interpolation, and one normal-flux continuity
          row is added per shared interior node."], "Notes", CellID->200000027],
Cell[BoxData["Region shorthands"], "NotesHead", CellID->200000028],
Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{"{Rectangle[{x1, y1}, {x2, y2}], yes}",
   "one patch, straight edges"},
{"{Annulus[{r1, r2}, {θ1, θ2}], yes}",
   "requires r1 > 0; one sector per π of arc"},
{"{Disk[...], NO}",
   "the polar map has J = 0 at r = 0; SpectralDomain::nreg"},
{"{Polygon[...], no}",
   "not decomposed automatically"}}]], "Notes", CellID->200000029],
Cell[BoxData["An annulus of angular span 2 π is two sectors, and the radial edges they
          share are detected as one interface. That call also raises
          SpectralDomain::iface, which reports that the pair of patches was matched
          along two different edges; the two-patch result and the shared edge count
          are both correct, so treat the message as information about the matching,
          not as a failure."], "Notes", CellID->200000030],
Cell[BoxData["Options"], "NotesHead", CellID->200000031],
Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{"{\"InterfaceTolerance\", 1*^-10}",
   "how far two edge traces may differ and still be one edge"},
{"{\"BoundaryPredicate\", Automatic}",
   "forces extra interior nodes to be Dirichlet; a node on a shared interface edge is refused by it"}}]], "Notes", CellID->200000032],
Cell[BoxData["Messages"], "NotesHead", CellID->200000033],
Cell[BoxData["SpectralDomain::nreg -- an unsupported region, Disk among them.
          SpectralDomain::iface -- edges matched within tolerance but the
          orientations disagree, or one pair of patches matched twice.
          SpectralDomain::patches -- the patch list contains something that is not a
          CoonsPatch."], "Notes", CellID->200000034]
}, Open]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData[{"Examples", "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]", Cell["(1)", "ExampleCount"]}],
  "PrimaryExamplesSection", CellTags->"PrimaryExamplesSection",
  CellID->200000035],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["Basic Examples"], "ExampleSection", "ExampleSection",
  WholeCellGroupOpener->True, CellID->200000036],
Cell["Set up a patch to discretize.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000037],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["edges = {Function[t, {2 t, -1}], Function[t, {2 t, 1}],
         Function[t, {-2, t}], Function[t, {2, t}]};
patch = CoonsPatch[edges];
None"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[1]:=", CellID->200000038]
}, Open]],
Cell["Discretizing a one-patch list gives a SpectralDiscretization object,
      recognized by SpectralDomainQ.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000039],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["disc = SpectralDomain[{patch}, 8];
{SpectralDomainQ[disc], disc[\"Type\"]}"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[2]:=", CellID->200000040],
Cell[BoxData["RowBox[{\"{\", RowBox[{\"True\", \",\", \"\\\"SpectralDiscretization\\\"\"}], \"}\"}]"], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[3]=", CellID->200000041]
}, Open]],
Cell["A rectangle needs no patches of your own.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000042],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["SpectralDomainData[SpectralDomain[Rectangle[{-1, -1}, {1, 1}], 6], \"PatchCount\"]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[4]:=", CellID->200000043],
Cell[BoxData["\"1\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[5]=", CellID->200000044]
}, Open]],
Cell["A half-annulus is one polar sector.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000045],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["SpectralDomainData[SpectralDomain[Annulus[{1, 2}, {0, Pi}], 6], \"PatchCount\"]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[6]:=", CellID->200000046],
Cell[BoxData["\"1\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[7]=", CellID->200000047]
}, Open]],
Cell["A full annulus is two sectors, coupled across their shared radial edges.
      The count is right; note the SpectralDomain::iface message, which
      reports that the pair of patches was matched along two different edges.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000048],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["SpectralDomainData[SpectralDomain[Annulus[{1, 2}, {0, 2 Pi}], 6], \"PatchCount\"]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[8]:=", CellID->200000049],
Cell[BoxData["\"2\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[9]=", CellID->200000050]
}, Open]],
Cell["The two sectors share one interface, so there are two interface pairs
      and two interface counts -- one interface per radial edge pair -- and
      the assembled system has 60 unknowns.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000051],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["ann2 = SpectralDomain[Annulus[{1, 2}, {0, 2 Pi}], 6];
{SpectralDomainData[ann2, \"PatchCount\"], Length[SpectralDomainData[ann2, \"InterfacePairs\"]],
 SpectralDomainData[ann2, \"InterfaceCount\"], SpectralDomainData[ann2, \"UnknownCount\"]}"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[10]:=", CellID->200000052],
Cell[BoxData["RowBox[{\"{\", RowBox[{\"2\", \",\", \"2\", \",\", \"2\", \",\", \"60\"}], \"}\"}]"], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[11]=", CellID->200000053]
}, Open]],
Cell["A disk is not supported, and says so. The polar map is singular at r =
      0, where the Jacobian is exactly 0 and the metric coefficients are
      infinite, so a disk would produce a silently wrong operator. Use
      Annulus[{r1, r2}, ...] with r1 > 0.", "ExampleText", CellID->200000054],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[BoxData["SpectralDomain[Disk[], 6]"], "Input", CellLabel->"In[12]:=", CellID->200000055],
Cell[BoxData["\"$Failed\""], "Output", CellLabel->"Out[13]=", CellID->200000056]
}, Open]]
}, Open]]
}, Open]],
